Work in the current working directory and complete this goal:

Act as a senior macOS/SwiftUI architect. Based on the repository context (msw is a shell CLI managing three persistent MicroSandbox VMs), design the best technical architecture for a small native macOS menu-bar app that monitors and controls msw. Cover status item APIs (MenuBarExtra vs NSStatusItem), process execution and environment discovery, JSON parsing, polling/streaming, concurrency/cancellation, launch-at-login, app sandbox/signing implications, notifications, deep links to Terminal/Ghostty/Zed/browser, and testability. Recommend a boring robust choice for a personal utility. Do not edit files or run project-wide tests/formatters/linters. Return an evidence-aware architecture memo and key implementation constraints.

Keep the change minimal and focused. Verify the work. Report a concise summary and every file changed.


**REQUIRED OUTPUT** — You MUST return ONLY a raw JSON object matching this schema:
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 20
    },
    "filesChanged": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      }
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "summary",
    "filesChanged"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
Do not include prose, markdown, headings, commentary, or code fences.
The first character of your response must be `{` and the last character must be `}`.
The workflow will fail unless the entire response is the JSON object.

